    {
      "kind": "speech",
      "language": "en",
      "voice": "af_heart",
      "text": "Imagine meeting someone away from the counter. Say hello and introduce yourself as Ana with the name expression. Returning to an earlier pattern after another topic lets you retrieve it without copying the previous model.",
      "text_sha256": "13050e580183bdf52e6e9719a3d6ba8bf8664df43b9e56b634ba44578f29a403",
      "audio_sha256": "8a4cf35cceab5a64ca9908dee486d2aa7f1c64596d559c59aafb164018b61964",
      "cacheFile": "11bf082e25ea8cb883e966f7fadc943c2bfba31bed29afd769333af0160128df.wav",
      "durationS": 14.825
    },
    {
      "kind": "silence",
      "seconds": 8
    },
    {
      "kind": "speech",
      "language": "pt",
      "voice": "pf_dora",
      "text": "Olá. Meu nome é Ana.",
      "text_sha256": "90c3d5cf56369379f51c83fef58ed2c0f4d45abcd2ca7b752e3ec6068e700cb7",
      "audio_sha256": "749b6fb3c33466497e3b1c11d83bcac899f4825b403cf1d363096608c8d2ca23",
      "cacheFile": "4e37e8917f82b836981161890f52e831639a23c32c554e8b5d64eafad18c7890.wav",
      "durationS": 1.725
    },
    {
      "kind": "silence",
      "seconds": 1.5
    },
    {
      "kind": "speech",
      "language": "en",
      "voice": "af_heart",
      "text": "Say I am Ana with the second identity expression. Compare it with the name expression from the previous turn. They share a purpose, but have different openings. Choose the requested opening during the pause.",
      "text_sha256": "a66100705a5c482d2dd5244323884bc531f27f08e44ecfb3e4428d214306c433",
      "audio_sha256": "04eb9beea0f10bd11e19e0b2fd1502f41decc1b24ad6a3c6179433284457506d",
      "cacheFile": "cad632473502f716b3bf850b9316791ee210c91353e14279b5d344cee526f77b.wav",
      "durationS": 13.725
    },
    {
      "kind": "silence",
      "seconds": 8
    },
    {
      "kind": "speech",
      "language": "pt",
      "voice": "pf_dora",
      "text": "Eu sou Ana.",
      "text_sha256": "596047442d69a4456a303c82c1e4d79fc432d5db47997f5047569c50509e0876",
      "audio_sha256": "7857b7764ab6a39d1d6d553143157044c13e898d445a8887c6d55bffc745ec18",
      "cacheFile": "d5e17d096fd0a5e2c2fa32c75fa42197f067e9604ebde08c7898efb1295c3e25.wav",
      "durationS": 1.35
    },
    {
      "kind": "silence",
      "seconds": 1.5
    },
    {
      "kind": "speech",
      "language": "en",
      "voice": "af_heart",
      "text": "Finally, say I would like a tea, please. After the model, try the same full request with coffee independently. Replay sections that need practice; a slow successful retrieval is useful progress toward speaking without an immediate example.",
      "text_sha256": "90d407fa47c97d5656f02304b70b9213b7c549587518a3168979d0f69fbaac6f",
      "audio_sha256": "33308baab34c4f395df50af5d6bbe13fbfecb87b49d1c723d910b067f0510c9c",
      "cacheFile": "0e0f739dac3c9daa636f0234112970c0f35600e0c45c36249644d9f885a96e96.wav",
      "durationS": 16.7
    },
    {
      "kind": "silence",
      "seconds": 8
    },
    {
      "kind": "speech",
      "language": "pt",
      "voice": "pf_dora",
      "text": "Eu gostaria de um chá, por favor.",
      "text_sha256": "3be67d0fe0adc12242cea949bc0a2407957f73f9bb73a1d4356ddeed2dcbe6c3",
      "audio_sha256": "56a3e7a7ca4d160c66ccad12b59899c20a76ac7cf2bb5cfcba98dd8dfb4260cb",
      "cacheFile": "203718a58decd058653e22790635e03c2a5bb44a9fc1c556496569018809f6da.wav",
      "durationS": 2.525
    },
    {
      "kind": "silence",
      "seconds": 1.5
    },
    {
      "kind": "speech",
      "language": "en",
      "voice": "af_heart",
      "text": "Let's add numbers. One is um. Two is dois. Three is três. Four is quatro. Five is cinco. Listen: um, dois, três, quatro, cinco. Dois sounds like the English word do — but it means two. Três sounds like the English word trace minus the e. Portuguese kept the Latin echoes.",
      "text_sha256": "010a6593dc8a9e69dde61b14ded16e17b16c3dabadcd94521f7eceb4638859a9",
      "audio_sha256": "4053c4eb6f561cb7335aeda19f22f005335df556c05d5724850188b991d08ade",
      "cacheFile": "b2e5e9b0a977303d1d90b8d7143b5cf117514df0f7eaf53b273e01fc28cd0e29.wav",
      "durationS": 20.9
    },
    {
      "kind": "silence",
      "seconds": 1
    },
    {
      "kind": "speech",
      "language": "pt",
      "voice": "pf_dora",
      "text": "Um, dois, três, quatro, cinco.",
      "text_sha256": "1ce3592e1744559ba59556508e90b0615367a875df23a6c78c6e26b44d4868d3",
      "audio_sha256": "0f7f48829110d2c4a798f7d4b12e8661bd5dac4ede818b8719ce73a162888c9e",
      "cacheFile": "f7e0d9fc2dcd8ab1fcee9b35d34e32a0588541b9b79c71ae80bbd24c077644a3.wav",
      "durationS": 2.275
    },
    {
      "kind": "silence",
      "seconds": 1.5
    },
    {
      "kind": "speech",
      "language": "en",
      "voice": "af_heart",
      "text": "Think. You want to say two coffees. Coffee is café. Two is dois. Build it: dois cafés. Three teas: três chás. The number doesn't change, only the noun. Same rule as Spanish, same logic you already know.",
      "text_sha256": "9845210e0a6eaeac901a0e98fa9279c080afe0bd72106aa86690a4cc6b618995",
      "audio_sha256": "b6bfa57e0af46fd9185a9646e6f6cab6b168a92b2d0397fda7b7e5219d2896e8",
      "cacheFile": "cf8ce489d9047adfa427c41f391fdf5ac4218dd802d266f6e7d0a6766aa36cf0.wav",
      "durationS": 15.25
    },
    {
      "kind": "silence",
      "seconds": 1
    },
    {
      "kind": "speech",
      "language": "pt",
      "voice": "pf_dora",
      "text": "Dois cafés. / Três chás.",
      "text_sha256": "45d23388b5f2ec8a1e7fc482129b7992eae2c5a0192c649f1d9036d22857b342",
      "audio_sha256": "d929fae0238743a93c548c666807b40a63749891b2d842527c3f403d09887080",
      "cacheFile": "f1d9bdced1b651ccf9a4b3910fa45b92dcfdd5c5b2e9dd9c976d1edab3e2375d.wav",
      "durationS": 1.925
    },
    {
      "kind": "silence",
      "seconds": 1.5
    },
    {
      "kind": "speech",
      "language": "en",
      "voice": "af_heart",
      "text": "Now time. Que horas são? means what time is it. The answer uses São as the verb. São duas means it is two o'clock. For one o'clock: é uma hora — singular. Two onward: são duas, são três. The same number system applied to the clock.",
      "text_sha256": "ba8d2f3b921fc3187c6ac8d6df5adbd3dbc9bb65b99b7292ac580f0f8f61a29c",
      "audio_sha256": "7c9dc1be54ea938c6bbb7970bbf6d9978e8d175d7c818b47013dc61f17805b3a",
      "cacheFile": "ace66788bc68fded0d7443390068e7eae76fa8b9b7ef7d5a355c50f7f8ee07d5.wav",
      "durationS": 17.35
    },
    {
      "kind": "silence",
      "seconds": 1
    },
    {
      "kind": "speech",
      "language": "pt",
      "voice": "pf_dora",
      "text": "Que horas são? São três.",
      "text_sha256": "e520ee67a38e9779c8907c6ecadeea1e46b74af0264655e8d299c1d85c7738d4",
      "audio_sha256": "e6dea2b03348ae2d2e5ee2c1c12b9772e31a54c3cd4771b7bd549a3e58f81f03",
      "cacheFile": "3f615cfc170b25932aa3a77eb6e58631c60e8700c58c776cf7f589cf7a4cb4c9.wav",
      "durationS": 1.825
    },
    {
      "kind": "silence",
      "seconds": 1.5
    },
    {
      "kind": "speech",
      "language": "en",
      "voice": "af_heart",
      "text": "Think. You have a class at four. São quatro. Your friend asks when. São quatro, you say. Now it's one o'clock — the singular. É uma hora. That's the only irregular. After that it's regular.",
